IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `roc-core`
IMPORT `roc-definitions`
IMPORT `roc4-order-19-div-1`

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), Order 19, Division 1 (rules 1 to 12): TESTS.
-- Every expected value is written from the text beside the assertion, before the run, and is not copied from the encoding's output.
-- Each timed rule is tested on both sides of the last day; the last day used is a made-up input (the lead's merge replaces it with O 3 r 3's answer).

-- Fixtures: the judgments appealed against.  Fields: court, who gave it, what it was given in, what began the proceedings, damages or accounts by a District Judge.
`o 19 test DC trial of an originating claim` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `District Court`, `A District Judge`, `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
`o 19 test MC absent-parties case on an originating claim` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `Magistrate's Court`, `A Magistrate`, `o 19 r 3(a) a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
`o 19 test DC trial of an originating application` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `District Court`, `A District Judge`, `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`, `Originating application`, FALSE
`o 19 test MC damages assessed by a District Judge` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `Magistrate's Court`, `A Magistrate`, `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken`, `Originating claim`, TRUE
`o 19 test MC damages not assessed by a District Judge` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `Magistrate's Court`, `A Magistrate`, `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
`o 19 test DC committal` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `District Court`, `A District Judge`, `o 19 r 3(c) an application for a committal order for contempt of court`, `Originating application`, FALSE
`o 19 test DC prerogative order` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `District Court`, `A District Judge`, `o 19 r 3(d) an application for a prerogative order`, `Originating application`, FALSE
`o 19 test GD judgment of a Judge` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `General Division`, `A Judge`, `o 19 r 3(a) a trial`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
`o 19 test GD judgment of the Registrar` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `General Division`, `The Registrar`, `o 19 r 3 any other decision`, `Originating claim`, FALSE
`o 19 test AD judgment` MEANS `o 19 r 1 judgment appealed against` OF `Appellate Division`, `A Judge`, `o 19 r 3(e) an appeal against a judgment described in paragraphs (a) to (d)`, `Originating claim`, FALSE

-- ===== Rule 1 =====
-- (a): a trial of an originating claim in a Magistrate's Court or District Court (i): yes.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test DC trial of an originating claim`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(i) "including a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent": yes.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test MC absent-parties case on an originating claim`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- (a)(i) says "an originating claim", so a trial of an originating application is not named: not covered.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test DC trial of an originating application`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(ii) after damages are assessed by a District Judge: yes; not by a District Judge: not named.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test MC damages assessed by a District Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test MC damages not assessed by a District Judge`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (a)(iii) committal for contempt: yes.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test DC committal`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A prerogative order is not in paragraph (a): not covered.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test DC prerogative order`) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A judgment of the General Division is not paragraph (a)'s.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test GD judgment of a Judge`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(a) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of a Magistrate's Court or District Court` `o 19 r 1 any other matter` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): a judgment of the General Division: yes; "except a judgment of the Registrar of the Supreme Court": no.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(b) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test GD judgment of a Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(b) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test GD judgment of the Registrar`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(b) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test DC trial of an originating claim`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(b) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the General Division` `o 19 r 1 any other matter` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (c): a judgment of the Appellate Division: yes; of the General Division: not paragraph (c)'s.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(c) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test AD judgment`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(c) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test GD judgment of a Judge`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(c) this Order applies to an appeal against a judgment of the Appellate Division` `o 19 r 1 any other matter` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (d): from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal pursuant to a written law: yes; not pursuant to a written law: not named.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(d) this Order applies to an appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal from a tribunal` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(d) this Order applies to an appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal from a tribunal` TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(d) this Order applies to an appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal from a tribunal` FALSE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(d) this Order applies to an appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `o 19 r 1 any other matter` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (e): an application relating to an appeal in (a) to (d): yes; not relating: not named.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(e) this Order applies to an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal` (`o 19 r 1 an application to the appellate Court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(e) this Order applies to an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal` (`o 19 r 1 an application to the appellate Court` FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(e) this Order applies to an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal` `o 19 r 1 any other matter` EQUALS NOTHING
-- (f): an appeal against an order of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act: yes.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(f) this Order applies to an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal` `o 19 r 1 an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1(f) this Order applies to an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal` `o 19 r 1 any other matter` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The gathered answer.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test DC trial of an originating claim`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test GD judgment of a Judge`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test AD judgment`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal from a tribunal` TRUE TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` (`o 19 r 1 an application to the appellate Court` TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` `o 19 r 1 an appeal against an order or decision of a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The Registrar's judgment is excepted from (b) and no other paragraph names it: no, in the words of the exception.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test GD judgment of the Registrar`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside the six paragraphs: not covered.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` (`o 19 r 1 an appeal against a judgment` `o 19 test DC prerogative order`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 1 this Order applies` `o 19 r 1 any other matter` EQUALS NOTHING

-- ===== Rule 2 =====
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(1) this Order yields to a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Paragraph (1) says what this Order yields to; with no such written law it is silent.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(1) this Order yields to a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Routes.  Fields: appealed from, appealed to, from a tribunal, from a Disciplinary Tribunal.
`o 19 test route DC to GD` MEANS `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF `District Court`, `General Division`, FALSE, FALSE
`o 19 test route MC to GD` MEANS `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF `Magistrate's Court`, `General Division`, FALSE, FALSE
`o 19 test route GD to AD` MEANS `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF `General Division`, `Appellate Division`, FALSE, FALSE
`o 19 test route GD to CA` MEANS `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF `General Division`, `Court of Appeal`, FALSE, FALSE
`o 19 test route tribunal to AD` MEANS `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF `General Division`, `Appellate Division`, TRUE, FALSE
`o 19 test route AD to CA` MEANS `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF `Appellate Division`, `Court of Appeal`, FALSE, FALSE
`o 19 test route DT to GD` MEANS `o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF `General Division`, `General Division`, FALSE, TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(2) Division 2 concerns the appeal from the District Court or the Magistrate's Court to the General Division` `o 19 test route DC to GD` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(2) Division 2 concerns the appeal from the District Court or the Magistrate's Court to the General Division` `o 19 test route MC to GD` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not named in paragraph (2): "concerns" does not say "only".
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(2) Division 2 concerns the appeal from the District Court or the Magistrate's Court to the General Division` `o 19 test route GD to AD` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(3)(a) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the General Division to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `o 19 test route GD to AD` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(3)(a) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the General Division to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `o 19 test route GD to CA` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(3)(a) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the General Division to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `o 19 test route DC to GD` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(3)(b) Division 3 concerns the appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `o 19 test route tribunal to AD` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(3)(b) Division 3 concerns the appeal from a tribunal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal` `o 19 test route GD to AD` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(3)(c) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal` `o 19 test route AD to CA` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(3)(c) Division 3 concerns the appeal from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal` `o 19 test route GD to CA` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(4) Division 4 concerns the appeal to the General Division from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` `o 19 test route DT to GD` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2(4) Division 4 concerns the appeal to the General Division from a Disciplinary Tribunal under the Medical Registration Act` `o 19 test route DC to GD` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2 the Division that concerns the appeal` `o 19 test route DC to GD` EQUALS `o 19 r 2 Division 2`
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2 the Division that concerns the appeal` `o 19 test route GD to CA` EQUALS `o 19 r 2 Division 3`
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2 the Division that concerns the appeal` `o 19 test route tribunal to AD` EQUALS `o 19 r 2 Division 3`
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2 the Division that concerns the appeal` `o 19 test route AD to CA` EQUALS `o 19 r 2 Division 3`
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2 the Division that concerns the appeal` `o 19 test route DT to GD` EQUALS `o 19 r 2 Division 4`
-- A route no paragraph names (District Court straight to the Court of Appeal) has no Division named.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 2 the Division that concerns the appeal` (`o 19 r 2 route of appeal` OF `District Court`, `Court of Appeal`, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS `o 19 r 2 no Division is named for the route`

-- ===== Rule 3 =====
-- "bundle of authorities": a compilation of authorities for the appeal.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is a bundle of authorities` `o 19 r 3 a compilation of authorities for the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is a bundle of authorities` `o 19 r 3 the notice of appeal` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "including case authorities, statutes and law journal articles": those three are in; the list is not closed.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 an item may be in a bundle of authorities` `o 19 r 3 a case authority` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 an item may be in a bundle of authorities` `o 19 r 3 a statute` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 an item may be in a bundle of authorities` `o 19 r 3 a law journal article` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 an item may be in a bundle of authorities` `o 19 r 3 any other item` EQUALS NOTHING
-- "core bundle of documents": the judgment copy, the extracted order, the compilation, the index.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of a core bundle of documents` `o 19 r 3 a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of a core bundle of documents` `o 19 r 3 the extracted order of the lower Court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of a core bundle of documents` `o 19 r 3 a compilation of the whole or part of the documents that are essential to the appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of a core bundle of documents` `o 19 r 3 an index cross-referencing each document to the record of appeal or supplemental record of appeal` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of a core bundle of documents` `o 19 r 3 the notice of appeal` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "judgment": (a) to (e) are judgments when the lower Court gave them; anything else is not.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` TRUE `o 19 r 3(a) a trial` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` TRUE `o 19 r 3(a) a case where judgment is given or the action is dismissed at trial because one or more parties are absent` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` TRUE `o 19 r 3(b) after damages are assessed or accounts are taken` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` TRUE `o 19 r 3(c) an application for a committal order for contempt of court` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` TRUE `o 19 r 3(d) an application for a prerogative order` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` TRUE `o 19 r 3(e) an appeal against a judgment described in paragraphs (a) to (d)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` TRUE `o 19 r 3 any other decision` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "a judgment given by the lower Court": one given by another court is not.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a decision is a judgment` FALSE `o 19 r 3(a) a trial` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "record of appeal".
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `o 19 r 3 the order granting permission to appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `o 19 r 3 the notice of appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `o 19 r 3 the certificate for security for costs` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `o 19 r 3 the record of proceedings` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `o 19 r 3 an affidavit of evidence-in-chief` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `o 19 r 3 another document filed in the lower Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "so far as are relevant to the matter decided and the nature of the appeal": an irrelevant document filed below is not part.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `o 19 r 3 another document filed in the lower Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of appeal` `o 19 r 3 a compilation of authorities for the appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "record of proceedings": the judgment copy, the extracted order, and the transcript in an appeal from the General Division, District Court or Magistrate's Court.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 19 r 3 a certified copy of the judgment or grounds of decision of the lower Court` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 19 r 3 the extracted order of the lower Court` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 19 r 3 the certified transcript of the official record of hearing taken at the hearing of the cause or matter` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 19 r 3 the certified transcript of the official record of hearing taken at the hearing of the cause or matter` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the record of proceedings` `o 19 r 3 the notice of appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "second core bundle": documents not in the appellant's or respondent's core bundle, with an index.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the second core bundle` `o 19 r 3 a compilation of the whole or part of the documents that are essential to the appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the second core bundle` `o 19 r 3 a compilation of the whole or part of the documents that are essential to the appeal` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the second core bundle` `o 19 r 3 an index cross-referencing each document to the record of appeal or supplemental record of appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a document is part of the second core bundle` `o 19 r 3 the notice of appeal` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "trial": the merits hearing and the applications heard with it or during it; anything else is not.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a proceeding is part of the trial` `o 19 r 3 the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a proceeding is part of the trial` `o 19 r 3 an application taken out or heard on the same day as such hearing` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a proceeding is part of the trial` `o 19 r 3 an application taken out or heard after the commencement of such hearing and before the judgment is given` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 3 a proceeding is part of the trial` `o 19 r 3 any other proceeding` EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- ===== Rule 4 =====
-- Scenario: the lower Court determined all matters other than costs on 1 March 2026; 30 days later is 31 March 2026.
-- (2)(a): each of (i) to (iv) is deemed to be a determination of costs; none of them is not.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 19 r 4(2)(a)(i) decided on the parties' entitlement to costs, even if the amount of costs or disbursements has not been determined` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 19 r 4(2)(a)(ii) ordered that costs be assessed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 19 r 4(2)(a)(iii) ordered that costs be reserved` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 19 r 4(2)(a)(iv) decided that there is to be no order as to costs or that each party is to bear its own costs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(a) the lower Court is deemed to have heard and determined the issue of costs` `o 19 r 4(2)(a) none of these` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (1): the time starts to run after the day everything including costs is determined.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (1A): costs decided on 31 March (within the 30 days): the paragraph does not apply.  On 1 April (after them): it applies.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1A) this paragraph applies` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 31 3 2026)) (Date 5 4 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1A) this paragraph applies` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) (Date 5 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Costs not yet determined: asked on 31 March the 30 days have not run out (not covered); asked on 1 April they have.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1A) this paragraph applies` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 31 3 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1A) this paragraph applies` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 4 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1A) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 1 4 2026)) (Date 5 4 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026)
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1A) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 31 3 2026)) (Date 5 4 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (2)(b): a bifurcated trial, a portion determined: the time for that portion starts after the date of that determination.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(b) this paragraph applies to a bifurcated portion` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(b) this paragraph applies to a bifurcated portion` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(b) this paragraph applies to a bifurcated portion` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(2)(b) the date after which the time for the filing starts to run for the bifurcated portion` (Date 20 3 2026) EQUALS JUST (Date 20 3 2026)
-- Gathered: costs on 15 March (within 30 days): after 15 March; costs on 10 April (after the 30 days): after 31 March; a written law or an order otherwise: not covered; costs not yet decided and asked on 20 March: not covered.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 15 3 2026)
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 4 2026)) (Date 20 4 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026)
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 20 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The "until" bar (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)): costs decided on 15 March.  On or before that day it holds; after it, it does not.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 16 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Costs not yet decided and the 30 days not yet run: the bar holds.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 20 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "unless the Court otherwise orders": no bar.  "Subject to any written law": not covered.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing cannot yet start to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 10 3 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- It never says time HAS started: JUST FALSE before the start date, NOTHING after it.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 10 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 16 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph (1A) is a positive start: all other matters were determined on 1 March, so the 30 days end on 31 March.
-- Costs still undecided: on the 30th day (31 March) the bar still holds; on the 31st day (1 April) time starts to run after the expiry of the 30-day period.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 4 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Paragraph (1A) is not made subject to a written law or to an order: the same day gives the same answer when either is raised.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 4 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 4 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Costs decided on 10 April, after the 30 days: time started after 31 March, whatever the later date of costs; before 31 March the bar holds.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 4 2026)) (Date 5 4 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 10 4 2026)) (Date 31 3 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Costs decided within the 30 days (15 March): (1A) does not apply, and the bar alone never says that time has started.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1) the time for the filing has started to run` (Date 1 3 2026) (JUST (Date 15 3 2026)) (Date 1 4 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The start-date function agrees on day 31, with or without a written law or an order.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4 the date after which the time for the filing starts to run` (Date 1 3 2026) NOTHING (Date 1 4 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 31 3 2026)
