-- ===== The helpers behind every timed function, and the rule 4(1A) period (added after a check that each layer-1 function has an assertion) =====
-- `o 19 r 8(3) the act is done by the last day`: done on the last day is in time; a day after is not; an extension moves the last day.
-- Last day 10 February 2026; extended to 17 February 2026.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the act is done by the last day` (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the act is done by the last day` (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the act is done by the last day` (Date 17 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (JUST (Date 17 2 2026)) EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the act is done by the last day` (Date 18 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (JUST (Date 17 2 2026)) EQUALS FALSE
-- `o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day`: both parts must be by the last day.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `o 19 r 8(3) the filing and the service are done by the last day` (Date 11 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) (Date 10 2 2026) NOTHING EQUALS FALSE
-- Rule 4(1A): the issue of costs is not heard and determined within 30 days after the other matters.
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1A) the period for the issue of costs`'s `period length` EQUALS 30
#ASSERT `o 19 r 4(1A) the period for the issue of costs`'s `period unit` EQUALS Days
